\\ arith.6502 - the race logic's 16-bit signed arithmetic, as the ST's 68000 does it (D9): a product's low
\\ word kept (muls.w, then move.w), a quotient rounded towards 0 (divs.w). Both take and give their number in
\\ num, so one's result is the next's input.

ZA_AUTO2 num                            ; mul_s16's and div_s16's number, in and out

\\ A signed 16-bit number times a small signed one: the product's low 16 bits.
\\
\\ Inputs:
\\     num: the number
\\     A: the multiplier, -127 to 127
\\
\\ Outputs:
\\     num: the product's low 16 bits
\\     A, Y: corrupted; X preserved

.mul_s16
{
    ZA_AUTO2 acc                        ; local: the sum
    ZA_AUTO1 m                          ; local: the multiplier's bits left
    ZA_AUTO1 neg                        ; local: bit 7, the multiplier's sign

    STA neg
    BPL @+
    EOR #&FF:INC A                      ; |multiplier|
.@
    STA m
    STZ acc:STZ acc+1
.bit
    LSR m
    BCC shift
    CLC
    LDA acc:ADC num:STA acc
    LDA acc+1:ADC num+1:STA acc+1
.shift
    ASL num:ROL num+1
    LDA m:BNE bit

    BIT neg:BMI negate
    LDA acc:STA num
    LDA acc+1:STA num+1
    RTS
.negate
    SEC
    LDA #0:SBC acc:STA num
    LDA #0:SBC acc+1:STA num+1
    RTS
}

\\ A signed 16-bit number divided by a positive one, the quotient rounded towards 0 (divs.w's). The
\\ quotient always fits: the divisor is at least 1 and the number at most 32,768 from 0.
\\
\\ Inputs:
\\     num: the number
\\     A: the divisor, 1 to 127
\\
\\ Outputs:
\\     num: the quotient
\\     A, Y: corrupted; X preserved

.div_s16
{
    ZA_AUTO1 d                          ; local: the divisor
    ZA_AUTO1 neg                        ; local: bit 7, the number's sign

    STA d
    LDA num+1:STA neg
    BPL @+
    SEC
    LDA #0:SBC num:STA num
    LDA #0:SBC num+1:STA num+1
.@
    LDA #0                              ; the remainder: under d, so it never carries out
    LDY #16
.bit
    ASL num:ROL num+1
    ROL A
    CMP d:BCC @+
    SBC d                               ; (C set)
    INC num                             ; (bit 0 clear after the shift)
.@
    DEY
    BNE bit

    BIT neg:BPL @+
    SEC
    LDA #0:SBC num:STA num
    LDA #0:SBC num+1:STA num+1
.@
    RTS
}
